    "journal.tbos.run.mode.ominous": "OMINOUS ×10",
    "floor.tbos.intro.subtitle.ominous": "OMINOUS ARCHIVE ×10 — TENFOLD REINFORCEMENTS",
    "message.tbos.archive.ominous_started": "OMINOUS ARCHIVE ×10 — Bad Omen consumed; this run is tenfold.",
    "message.tbos.shrine.discovered.observatory": "The Observatory still watches a conjunction that will not set.",
    "message.tbos.shrine.discovered.curator_workshop": "The Curator Workshop keeps a bronze frame waiting for its glass.",
    "message.tbos.shrine.discovered.evacuation_gate": "The Evacuation Gate still holds the last hour of leaving.",
    "message.tbos.coffer.already_opened": "This coffer has already been recalled.",
    "message.tbos.coffer.recovered.observatory": "The Observatory coffer yields a cracked Lens and the last archivist's notes.",
    "message.tbos.coffer.recovered.curator_workshop": "The Workshop coffer yields a cracked Lens and the last archivist's notes.",
    "message.tbos.coffer.recovered.evacuation_gate": "The Evacuation coffer yields a cracked Lens and the last archivist's notes.",
    "message.tbos.archive.no_sleep": "There is no night in a day that never ended.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.0": "Wake-light still clings to the first catalogue.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.1": "Portraits that never finished being painted.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.2": "A meridian that remembers falling.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.3": "Hours sung to an empty choir.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.4": "Glass that kept more than light.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.5": "Shelves that index a missing day.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.6": "The Cantor's maze still keeps time.",
    "floor.tbos.intro.blurb.7": "The hour that was never written down.",
    "tome.tbos.page_indicator": "%s / %s",
    "tome.tbos.hint": "Click either side of the page to turn it.",
    "tome.tbos.page.0": "The orrery was never decoration. We steered living rings through a measured conjunction and filed each orbit as it passed. If the rings still move when you recall them, the work is unfinished.",
    "tome.tbos.page.1": "The Curator was bronze and glass, repaired more often than it was praised. A smith set a new mechanism into its chest the morning of the last day. It was built to keep order, not to choose it.",
    "tome.tbos.page.2": "A family stood under the Archive roof and watched a captured star cross. They were not archivists. The record kept them anyway. Some visitors become catalogue.",
    "tome.tbos.page.3": "When the halls began to fail we ran for the Meridian. We were still writing as we left. If you find our notes in a shrine, we did not have time to come back for them.",
    "tome.tbos.page.4": "The last order was simple: preserve this day forever. The Curator heard it. The Archive obeyed. Forever is longer than we meant.",
    "tome.tbos.page.5": "The rings stopped. The pillars leaned. One second refused to end, and we are still inside it. What you call ruin is the page. What you call remembered is the ink still wet.",
    "message.tbos.archive.room_intro": "Floor %s · Room %s/%s · %s",
